{
 "regions": {
  "r2": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "blindness: oh the impudence of the body ! It is still afraid of",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "being overtaken by death.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r3": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "11. Desire is, indeed, a river, with the objects of desire",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "for its water, agitated by waves in the form of hankerings,",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "having for sharks the passions, and for birds the misgivings",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "( of the heart ), destroying the tree of fortitude, difficult to",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "cross on account of eddies in the form of infatuation, very",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "deep and having anxiety for its steep (lit. high) banks; the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "great ascetics of pure heart, who have crossed it (the river),",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 8,
     "text": "enjoy felicity.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r4": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "12. I do not expect the course of life in this world to",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "turn out happy; the result of meritorious deeds inspires me",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "with fear as I contemplate it; for, enjoyments, long experi-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "enced in return for accumulated stores of merit, assume",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "mighty proportions to make the enjoyer miserable, as it were.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r5": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "13. Even after remaining with one for a long time",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "pleasures must needs vanish. What more is there in plea-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "sures tearing themselves off from one, that one does not of",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "one’s own accord relinquish them? When vanishing of",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "their own accord, they end in keen anguish for the mind;",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 8,
     "text": "but when relinquished by one of one’s own will, they pro-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 9,
     "text": "duce infinite happiness proceeding from tranquillity.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r6": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "14. Those, who, by the knowledge of Brahman, have",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "acquired discrimination and possess a refined intellect, do",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "what is hard to do, in that they renounce riches even such",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "as contribut to pleasures, being absolutely unselfish: (these)",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "were neither obtained before, nor are they now; nor is there",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "any certainty ( lit. firm belief ) as to their attainment; and",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "still we are not able to renounce them, although their posses-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 8,
     "text": "sion ( lit. desire ) is only a matter of imagination.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r7": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "15. Of the blessed persons who dwell in the caves of",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "mountains and contemplate the Supreme Light, birds drink",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r1": {
